Task: Redesign Cart as line items, remove generated Postgres implementation (Phase 1 of redis-cart-model_20261002)

Summary: Replaced the generated Cart/CartStore (id/createdAt/updatedAt only, every
field-substitution point an unfilled codegen placeholder) with a hand-designed
line-item model: Cart(id, items: Map[String, Int], createdAt, updatedAt) and a
CartStore[F] algebra (create/get/addItem/removeItem/setQuantity/delete/ping). Deleted
the entire generated Postgres implementation (CartStore.postgres, Migrations.scala,
MigrationsSuite, CartStorePostgresSuite, the Flyway migration SQL, PostgresConfig) and
its skunk/flyway/flyway-database-postgresql/postgresql-JDBC build.sbt dependencies,
plus the otel4s dependencyOverrides block that existed only to resolve Skunk's otel4s
conflict. Trimmed CartRoutes to drop the PATCH/PUT whole-cart-update endpoints (no
generic "update" exists against a line-item model) and removed the now-pointless
CreateCartRequest body (create() takes no params) - create/get/delete remain a thin
resource shell; add/remove-item HTTP endpoints are the cart-items_20261002 track's job.
Main.scala temporarily wires CartStore.inMemory pending this track's own Phase 2/3
Redis implementation.

